WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.434 align:start size:94% position:6%
-We're here with our frien
Henry Winkler.

00:00:01.434 --> 00:00:03.770 size:78% position:39%
Is this a true story?
We were talking about

00:00:03.770 --> 00:00:05.505 align:start size:94% position:6%
your grandson
dressing up like The Fonz --

00:00:05.505 --> 00:00:08.842 align:start size:94% position:6%
that the leather jacket
was not originally

00:00:08.842 --> 00:00:11.611 align:start size:94% position:6%
going to be part
of the iconic costume?

00:00:11.611 --> 00:00:16.049 align:start size:94% position:6%
-No, I --
I had to wear a golf jacket.

00:00:16.049 --> 00:00:18.151 line:92%
It was a McGregor golf jacket.

00:00:18.151 --> 00:00:21.354 align:start size:94% position:6%
It was puce, and I --
-[ Laughs ]

00:00:21.354 --> 00:00:22.455 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You know,
I've said this before,

00:00:22.455 --> 00:00:25.225 align:start size:94% position:6%
but it's very hard
to be cool in puce.

00:00:25.225 --> 00:00:26.626 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes.
-I just want to say.

00:00:26.626 --> 00:00:29.462 align:start size:94% position:6%
And the collar
would not stay up,

00:00:29.462 --> 00:00:35.602
because ABC thought I was goin
to be associated with crime.

00:00:35.602 --> 00:00:37.971 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Right. This is the times
we're living in,

00:00:37.971 --> 00:00:40.473 line:92%
that leather meant crime.

00:00:40.473 --> 00:00:42.075 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Exactly.
-Yeah.

00:00:42.075 --> 00:00:44.844 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Leather
and a T-shirt together...

00:00:44.844 --> 00:00:47.380 line:92%
-Yeah, that's a crime spree.

00:00:47.380 --> 00:00:51.151 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And then, I had on
engineer boots that I wore

00:00:51.151 --> 00:00:54.320 align:start size:94% position:6%
in "The Lords of Flatbush,
'cause I like to bring

00:00:54.320 --> 00:00:58.291 align:start size:94% position:6%
something from
one project to another.

00:00:58.291 --> 00:01:02.929
Then, Gary Marshall went to AB
and said, "You know, The Fon

00:01:02.929 --> 00:01:07.267 align:start size:94% position:6%
could be hurt
if he was in a cycle accident.

00:01:07.267 --> 00:01:10.136 align:start size:94% position:6%
And they said,
"If you do a scene

00:01:10.136 --> 00:01:14.707 align:start size:94% position:6%
with his bike,
he can wear leather."

00:01:14.707 --> 00:01:17.710 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And that was it?
-And that was it.

00:01:17.710 --> 00:01:18.344 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Then slowly but --

00:01:18.344 --> 00:01:23.016 align:start size:94% position:6%
That's why you see me wheeling
the bike in to Arnold's.

00:01:23.016 --> 00:01:26.820 align:start size:94% position:6%
That it is in the living roo
of the Cunninghams,

00:01:26.820 --> 00:01:29.389 align:start size:94% position:6%
in my apartment
above the garage.

00:01:29.389 --> 00:01:32.225 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I see. So you just had
to have the bike everywhere.

00:01:32.225 --> 00:01:34.094 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes, I had
to have the bike everywhere.

00:01:34.094 --> 00:01:36.329 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then, eventually,
they let that go,

00:01:36.329 --> 00:01:40.300 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I was very fortunate,
years later,

00:01:40.300 --> 00:01:42.469 align:start size:94% position:6%
to give the jacket
to the Smithsonian.

00:01:42.469 --> 00:01:46.639 align:start size:94% position:6%
-A very -- If anything deserve
to be there, it's that.

00:01:46.639 --> 00:01:50.009
Now, Henry, we've talked about
that you like trout fishing,

00:01:50.009 --> 00:01:54.013 align:start size:94% position:6%
and based on these photos,
I can't tell...

00:01:54.013 --> 00:01:56.783 align:start size:94% position:6%
I can't tell if you really do.
Do you really?

00:01:56.783 --> 00:01:58.618 align:start size:94% position:6%
Do you really like
trout fishing?

00:01:58.618 --> 00:01:59.752 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:59.752 --> 00:02:03.389 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Now, I want to tell you.
I would love --

00:02:03.389 --> 00:02:04.290 line:92%
See, you know what that is

00:02:04.290 --> 00:02:08.128 align:start size:94% position:6%
That is a cutthroat
and a rainbow.

00:02:08.128 --> 00:02:11.131 size:84% position:42%
They mated, and that is
a hybrid right there.

00:02:11.131 --> 00:02:13.266 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That's a hybrid?
-Isn't that beautiful?

00:02:13.266 --> 00:02:15.368 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It's beautiful.
-That is a beautiful fish.

00:02:15.368 --> 00:02:16.369 line:92%
And then, I give it a kiss

00:02:16.369 --> 00:02:18.138 align:start size:94% position:6%
I take a picture,
and give it back.

00:02:18.138 --> 00:02:20.039 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, so you don't
eat your trout?

00:02:20.039 --> 00:02:23.276
-I've never -- I won't eve
eat a trout in a restaurant.

00:02:23.276 --> 00:02:26.045 size:84% position:42%
-Really? Even when it's
too late for the trout?

00:02:26.045 --> 00:02:28.748
-I think -- You know what?
I think they're so majestic,

00:02:28.748 --> 00:02:31.551 align:start size:94% position:6%
and if I --
I love trout fishing,

00:02:31.551 --> 00:02:34.921
but if I could, I wish --
You know, when they --

00:02:34.921 --> 00:02:38.625 align:start size:94% position:6%
when you show them all playing
their instruments before,

00:02:38.625 --> 00:02:41.661 align:start size:94% position:6%
you know, at home, the band?
-Yeah.

00:02:41.661 --> 00:02:44.597 size:78% position:39% line:92%
-I wish I could sing.

00:02:44.597 --> 00:02:46.966 size:78% position:39% line:92%
-What would you sing?

00:02:46.966 --> 00:02:47.667 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-I would sing --

00:02:47.667 --> 00:02:49.936 align:start size:94% position:6%
Well, I would sing
a combination.

00:02:49.936 --> 00:02:58.945
The Boss, Bruno Mars, Ben Platt,
Sia, and Brandi Carlile.

00:02:58.945 --> 00:03:00.013 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:00.013 --> 00:03:03.383
-I cannot believe how much
thought you put into that.

00:03:03.383 --> 00:03:07.487 align:start size:94% position:6%
-No, I -- just they are
on my mind and on my iPod.

00:03:07.487 --> 00:03:10.323 size:88% position:44%
-I mean, five winners --
five winners in a row.

00:03:10.323 --> 00:03:12.058 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, my God.
They're so good.

00:03:12.058 --> 00:03:15.395
-Hey, last time you were here,
you had just finished shooting

00:03:15.395 --> 00:03:18.464 align:start size:94% position:6%
the Wes Anderson film
that just premiered at Cannes,

00:03:18.464 --> 00:03:21.034
"The French Dispatch."
I'm so excited to see it.

00:03:21.034 --> 00:03:22.302 align:start size:94% position:6%
I always look forward
to his films.

00:03:22.302 --> 00:03:25.371 align:start size:94% position:6%
It must have been thrillin
to do.

00:03:25.371 --> 00:03:29.842 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You learn the language of Wes
You really do.

00:03:29.842 --> 00:03:32.345 size:75% position:38% line:92%
He is very specific.

00:03:32.345 --> 00:03:35.782 align:start size:94% position:6%
Bob Balaban
was my brother in it.

00:03:35.782 --> 00:03:36.883 size:88% position:44% line:92%
We're brothers together.

00:03:36.883 --> 00:03:39.852 align:start size:94% position:6%
I can't even
show you a picture yet.

00:03:39.852 --> 00:03:43.156 line:92%
But I whispered to Bob, I said

00:03:43.156 --> 00:03:46.759 align:start size:94% position:6%
"I have an idea.
Should I ask Wes?"

00:03:46.759 --> 00:03:50.296 align:start size:94% position:6%
And he said
out of the side of his mouth

00:03:50.296 --> 00:03:53.132 align:start size:94% position:6%
"No," and so I didn't.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:53.132 --> 00:03:56.536 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then, Benicio del Toro
was in our set,

00:03:56.536 --> 00:03:58.238 line:92%
and we went to dinner together

00:03:58.238 --> 00:04:01.007 align:start size:94% position:6%
They are just
lovely human beings.

00:04:01.007 --> 00:04:05.878 align:start size:94% position:6%
And Tilda Swinton,
who is, like, this icon

00:04:05.878 --> 00:04:09.515 line:92%
of independence in the world

00:04:09.515 --> 00:04:13.086 align:start size:94% position:6%
Just wonderful.
-Oh, that is so lovely to hear

00:04:13.086 --> 00:04:15.955
Now, I want to finish tonight --
We used to have a traditio

00:04:15.955 --> 00:04:17.323 align:start size:94% position:6%
back in the days
when we were all here.

00:04:17.323 --> 00:04:19.292 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's called "$5 Friday."
You remember.

00:04:19.292 --> 00:04:21.327 align:start size:94% position:6%
I don't need to tell you.
-I do. I do.

00:04:21.327 --> 00:04:24.397 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And you were here on a da
we did it,

00:04:24.397 --> 00:04:28.334 align:start size:94% position:6%
and you put your $5 in, and we
still have it right here.

00:04:28.334 --> 00:04:31.170 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'd like to show you.
This is the Henry Winkler $5

00:04:31.170 --> 00:04:33.439 size:75% position:38%
And what happens is,
we spin this around,

00:04:33.439 --> 00:04:35.508 align:start size:94% position:6%
and we take out the winner
and they get the money.

00:04:35.508 --> 00:04:38.344 align:start size:94% position:6%
Now, when you were here,
Henry, you won.

00:04:38.344 --> 00:04:41.447 align:start size:94% position:6%
You're -- it's the first tim
a guest had ever won,

00:04:41.447 --> 00:04:45.785 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I'll let you
tell everybody what you did.

00:04:45.785 --> 00:04:48.087 line:92%
-Well, I was in a limousine,

00:04:48.087 --> 00:04:53.059 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I was on my way
to do "Actor's Studio."

00:04:53.059 --> 00:04:54.294 line:92%
"Inside the Actor's Studio."

00:04:54.294 --> 00:04:58.364 align:start size:94% position:6%
I was never invited,
and so finally I was invited

00:04:58.364 --> 00:05:01.100 align:start size:94% position:6%
to do an interview
with Alec Baldwin.

00:05:01.100 --> 00:05:05.238 align:start size:94% position:6%
Got the call, "You won,"
and I asked how much it was.

00:05:05.238 --> 00:05:08.207 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I think it was $190.
-Yeah.

00:05:08.207 --> 00:05:11.844 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It was such a hard decision..
[ Laughter ]

00:05:11.844 --> 00:05:18.718 align:start size:94% position:6%
...not to take the money,
but I decided, "You know what?

00:05:18.718 --> 00:05:24.157
Traffic in New York, and I -
Monday -- This was a Friday.

00:05:24.157 --> 00:05:28.328 size:88% position:44%
Monday, treat the crew
to whatever they wanted.

00:05:28.328 --> 00:05:30.396 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Right.
-And I think you had pizza

00:05:30.396 --> 00:05:32.398 align:start size:94% position:6%
-We had pizza.
We always respect

00:05:32.398 --> 00:05:35.535 align:start size:94% position:6%
that you gave yourself
the weekend to think it over

00:05:35.535 --> 00:05:36.502 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:05:36.502 --> 00:05:37.403 align:start size:94% position:6%
All right.
So here we go.

00:05:37.403 --> 00:05:40.640 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's $5 Friday again.
We want to see if Henry Winkle

00:05:40.640 --> 00:05:41.407 size:88% position:44% line:92%
has the luck he deserves

00:05:41.407 --> 00:05:43.242 align:start size:94% position:6%
for being the nicest man
in show business.

00:05:43.242 --> 00:05:47.880 align:start size:94% position:6%
But this time
the winner is Arbulu.

00:05:47.880 --> 00:05:49.148 size:88% position:44% line:92%
Christine is the winner.

00:05:49.148 --> 00:05:52.285
And knowing Christine,
there will be no pizza...

00:05:52.285 --> 00:05:53.486 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:05:53.486 --> 00:05:59.525 align:start size:94% position:6%
...but we do look forward
to her new clothes on Monday

00:05:59.525 --> 00:06:00.426 line:92%
Thank you so much, Henry.

00:06:00.426 --> 00:06:04.430 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Monsters at Work" is currentl
streaming on Disney+.

